## How to use it

**Add an external reference (article, doc, video):**
```
/wiki-update <url>
```

**Search for prior work:**
```
/wiki-search "what query"
```

**End-of-session (development projects):**
```
/wrap-up
```
Distills the session into proposed wiki entries. Stages to `wiki/_inbox/proposed/`. You review + promote.

**Full ingest cycle (research projects):**
```
/wiki-cycle
```
Discover → ingest → lint → promote → commit. Default behavior is conservative; flags like `--full`, `--ingest-only`, `--lint-only` change scope.

## Best-practices folder

`best-practices/` was seeded from the bootstrap installer's curated set — software-dev best practices that apply across projects (coding, communication, documentation, logging, testing, etc.). It travels with every install.

These are **reference**, not part of the curated wiki. Read them, link to them from `wiki/` entries when relevant. Don't edit them by hand — if you want to override the canonical version for this project, copy the file into `wiki/best-practices/` (project-specific folder) and customize there.

## How-to folder

`how-to/` has short usage docs for the commands above. Start with `how-to/getting-started.md`.

## Don't

- Don't hand-edit `_MAP.md` or `_INDEX.md` — they're auto-generated by `wiki-map-compile.py` and `wiki-index-per-folder.py`
- Don't suppress contradictions in `wiki/` — both-sides-stay: keep contradictory entries cross-linked, never delete the minority view
- Don't promote directly to `wiki/` — always stage through `wiki/_inbox/proposed/` and use `/wiki-promote` to move

